    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project a balanced offensive attack today, with **Jackson Merrill** leading the charge at a 62.07 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Nola yields a significant platoon edge (+13%), making him our premier option despite the risk of moderate speed suppression. Close behind is **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.14), whose ability to drive the ball provides a high floor, and **Kyle Tucker** (61.08), who remains a locked-in asset against Soroka. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also earns a strong 61.04 start; while he faces a solid arm in Bachar, his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the promotion to the two-hole make him a high-leverage play for both run production and his essential stolen base upside.\n\nOn the bench, **Coby Mayo** was the most difficult exclusion, posting a 48.16 score. While his platoon adjustment against Early was positive, he ultimately lacked the volume and ceiling required to displace veterans like **Miguel Vargas** or **Curtis Mead** in our crowded infield. We are keeping a close eye on **Josh Jung** (52.42), whose score reflects a notable 5% deduction due to wind-in conditions, adding a layer of risk to his otherwise favorable spot in the order. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** as he remains on the IL, though we look forward to the eventual return of depth pieces like **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Heliot Ramos** to provide further flexibility. For tonight, owners should remain cautious with **Liam Hicks** (45.50), as the dynamic platoon penalty against Lovelady significantly compresses his utility compared to our primary starting core.",
